From 4d2a74ed9c5b9347132f69a0191a55654a526bc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:41:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): restore nightly lifecycle probes and preserve
 observer cooldown [daveey]

Nightly subprocess lifecycle homes lacked class routing after model-neutral
admission became mandatory. Provision real fast/standard/deep registries and
dummy custom credentials confined to a literal loopback endpoint; keep the
real dispatcher, owner, allocator, credential pool and failure observer.

A second defect was hidden behind the zero-launch failures: managed exec
removed the documented host cooldown knob before arming the result observer,
which then persisted a 300s episode despite a zero-cooldown dispatcher.
Preserve only that exact operational name, retaining task/unknown-secret
exclusion. Use a short future Retry-After rather than an expired zero hint.

Request class:deep review rather than a mandatory concrete provider/model;
prove same-model reviewer runs in a separate admitted session. Expand event
diagnostics so future admission/episode failures remain readable.

Verification: original worker-contract RED 4 failures; managed-env RED 7 pass,
2 failures for zero/nonzero cooldown; focused GREEN and 13-file consumer
sweep GREEN with file retries disabled. Full scripts/check passes.

Hermes-Card: t_a652313fa13f477c
